window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e0f092cc982945c2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"data-and-connections\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">数据与连接</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>你的网站可能需要保存请求、记住进度，或展示来自已连接应用的信息。请告诉 ChatGPT 要保存什么、信息来自哪里，以及谁应该拥有访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-supported-site-shape\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choose-storage-and-sign-in-features\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择存储和登录功能</h2> <p>对于新项目，Sites 工作流可以从推荐的网站起始模板开始。对于现有项目，在请求部署之前，请先让 ChatGPT 确认该项目能生成兼容的部署产物。</p> <p>描述网站应该如何工作，让 ChatGPT 据此选择所需的存储和身份验证功能：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>网站需求</th> <th>应向 Sites 提出的要求</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>以内容展示为主的网站或落地页</td> <td>除非体验确实需要，否则不保存持久化的应用状态</td> </tr> <tr> <td>保存记录、用户进度或游戏分数</td> <td>使用 D1（一种用于持久化结构化数据的关系型数据库）</td> </tr> <tr> <td>图片、文档、音频、视频或其他上传内容</td> <td>使用 R2（一种用于存储文件的对象存储服务）</td> </tr> <tr> <td>带有可搜索元数据的上传文件</td> <td>用 D1 保存元数据，用 R2 保存文件内容</td> </tr> <tr> <td>需要识别当前工作区用户的内部网站</td> <td>使用通过工作区身份验证的用户身份</td> </tr> <tr> <td>公开登录，或使用外部身份提供方</td> <td>启用身份验证的网站</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>不要为临时的展示状态请求持久化存储，例如主题选择或已关闭的横幅。对于用户期望托管网站能够记住的产品数据，则应请求持久化存储。</p> <p><a id=\"add-sign-in-with-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"sign-in-with-chatgpt\">添加 Sign in with ChatGPT</h2> <p>公开网站可以继续向所有人开放，同时提供可选的 Sign in with ChatGPT，以支持需要识别用户身份的功能，例如保存进度、个性化视图，或归属于特定用户的记录。仅限工作区访问的网站已经使用 ChatGPT 身份来执行其共享设置。</p> <p>请让 Sites 添加登录体验：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">为这个公开网站添加“使用 ChatGPT 登录”功能。未登录访客仍可访问。访客未登录时，显示“使用 ChatGPT 登录”操作。登录后，如果有全名就用全名问候；否则使用其电子邮件地址。添加“退出登录”操作，并确保授权判断由服务器端代码执行。\n</code></pre> <p><strong>工作方式</strong></p> <p>Sites 会通过平台提供的路径处理登录和登出流程，然后将访客带回你的网站：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;a href=\"/signin-with-chatgpt\"&gt;Sign in with ChatGPT&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;a href=\"/signout-with-chatgpt\"&gt;Sign out&lt;/a&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>访客登录后，Sites 会通过以下请求标头将其身份信息传递给服务器：</p> <ul> <li><code>oai-authenticated-user-email</code> 包含经过身份验证的电子邮件地址。</li> <li><code>oai-authenticated-user-full-name</code> 可能包含非空的个人资料名称。请将其视为可选字段；如果没有名称，则回退使用电子邮件地址。</li> </ul> <p>请在服务器端代码中执行授权判断，不要依赖把姓名拆分开的标头。</p> <p><a id=\"load-visitor-data-via-plugins\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"bring-user-data-to-your-site-with-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">使用插件将用户数据带入网站</h2> <p>在 Sites 中使用插件，可以构建从每位网站访客自己的已连接应用中加载数据的网站。例如，问题跟踪看板可以向你展示分配给你的问题，并向队友展示分配给他们的问题。每位访客都要使用 ChatGPT 登录，并选择允许访问哪些已连接账户以及相应权限。</p> <p>工作区必须启用插件使用功能，而且网站必须设为仅对该工作区开放。访客必须属于该工作区，并使用他们现有的应用权限。管理员可以在<a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?sectionMissing=enable-plugin-use-in-sites\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">为 Sites 启用插件使用（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>中查看每个插件的权限和租户限制。</p> <p><a id=\"build-a-site-with-connected-data\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">使用已连接的数据构建网站</h3> <ol> <li>让 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 构建一个网站。说出要使用的插件连接器及其用途，或询问当前有哪些插件可用。</li> <li>使用真实数据试用预览。代理在构建和预览网站时会使用你已有的连接。</li> <li>让代理为你的工作区发布网站，并将链接分享给队友。</li> </ol> <p>例如：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用我已连接的问题跟踪工具构建一个网站，显示分配给我的问题并按优先级分组。添加项目筛选器、指向原始问题的链接和“刷新”按钮。\n</code></pre> <p>你还可以构建文档查找器，让它链接到原始文档；也可以创建项目概览，同时汇总工单和消息。</p> <p><a id=\"data-loading\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">加载数据</h3> <p>页面加载时，Sites 会使用访客自己的连接和权限读取已连接的数据。Sites 会管理缓存和重新加载；如有需要，可以让 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 添加手动刷新操作。</p> <p>默认情况下，如果连接器返回了分页游标，Sites 会使用 <strong>Load more（加载更多）</strong>操作来获取下一页。</p> <p><strong>技术参考：插件发现</strong></p> <p>Sites 使用 <code>getContext()</code> 查找插件的操作。它会返回缓存的工具名称、描述和参数结构定义；不会刷新插件发现结果。</p> <p>有关支持的已连接应用操作及其可用性，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建和使用 ChatGPT Sites（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"let-visitors-choose-their-connections\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">让访客选择连接</h3> <p>要使用已连接功能，访客需要使用 ChatGPT 登录，查看网站请求的应用访问权限，选择允许连接的账户和权限，然后返回网站。分享网站并不会授予访客访问你所连接账户的权限。网站只会收到每位访客所允许的应用数据。</p> <p>访客可以不授予应用访问权限而继续使用网站，但依赖这些权限的功能将无法工作。如果某个应用不可用，请检查它是否已连接到正确的工作区，以及是否得到工作区设置的允许。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"data-and-connections\">Data and connections</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Your site might need to save requests, remember progress, or show information from connected apps. Tell ChatGPT what to save, where the information comes from, and who should have access.</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-supported-site-shape\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"choose-storage-and-sign-in-features\">Choose storage and sign-in features</h2> <p>For new projects, the sites workflow can start with its recommended site starter. For an existing project, ask ChatGPT to confirm that the project can produce compatible deployment artifacts before you request a deployment.</p> <p>Describe what the site should do so ChatGPT can choose the required storage and identity features:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Site need</th> <th>What to ask sites for</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Content-led website or landing page</td> <td>A site with no persistent application state unless the experience requires it</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Saved records, user progress, or game scores</td> <td>D1, a relational database for durable structured data</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Images, documents, audio, video, or other uploads</td> <td>R2, object storage for files</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Uploaded files with searchable metadata</td> <td>D1 for metadata and R2 for file contents</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Internal site that needs the current workspace user's identity</td> <td>Workspace-authenticated user identity</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Public sign-in or an external identity provider</td> <td>An authentication-enabled site</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Don't request durable storage for temporary presentation state, such as a theme choice or a dismissed banner. Do request it for product data that people expect the hosted site to remember.</p> <h2 id=\"add-sign-in-with-chatgpt\">Add Sign in with ChatGPT</h2> <p>Public sites can remain open to everyone while offering optional Sign in with ChatGPT for identity-aware features, such as saved progress, personalized views, or records that belong to a specific person. Workspace-restricted sites already use ChatGPT identity to enforce their sharing settings.</p> <p>Ask sites to add the sign-in experience:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add Sign in with ChatGPT to this public site. Keep the site available to signed-out visitors. Show a Sign in with ChatGPT action when someone is signed out. After they sign in, greet them with their full name when available, or their email address otherwise. Add a Sign out action, and keep authorization decisions in server-side code.\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"how-it-works\"></a> <strong>How it works</strong></p> <p>Sites handles the sign-in and sign-out flows through platform-provided paths, then returns the visitor to your site:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;a href=\"/signin-with-chatgpt\"&gt;Sign in with ChatGPT&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;a href=\"/signout-with-chatgpt\"&gt;Sign out&lt;/a&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>After a visitor signs in, sites forwards their identity to the server through these request headers:</p> <ul> <li><code>oai-authenticated-user-email</code> contains the authenticated email address.</li> <li><code>oai-authenticated-user-full-name</code> may contain a non-empty profile name. Treat it as optional and fall back to the email address.</li> </ul> <p>Keep authorization decisions in server-side code, and don't depend on name-split headers.</p> <p><a id=\"load-visitor-data-via-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"bring-user-data-to-your-site-with-plugins\">Bring user data to your site with plugins</h2> <p>Use plugins in sites to build a site that loads data from each site viewer's own connected apps. For example, an issue dashboard can show your assigned issues to you and your teammate's assigned issues to them. Each visitor signs in with ChatGPT and chooses which connected accounts and access to allow.</p> <p>Plugin use must be enabled in the workspace, and the site must be private to that workspace. Visitors need to belong to the workspace and use their existing app permissions. Admins can review individual plugin permissions and tenant restrictions in <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?sectionMissing=enable-plugin-use-in-sites\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Enable plugin use in sites (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"build-a-site-with-connected-data\">Build a site with connected data</h3> <ol> <li>Ask ChatGPT Work or Codex to build a site. Name the plugin connector and what it should do, or ask which plugins are available.</li> <li>Try the preview with real data. The agent uses your available connections while building and previewing the site.</li> <li>Ask the agent to publish the site for your workspace and share its link with teammates.</li> </ol> <p>For example:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a site using my connected issue tracker that shows issues assigned to me, grouped by priority. Add project filters, links to the original issues, and a Refresh button.\n</code></pre> <p>You can also build a document finder that links to original documents or a project overview that combines tickets and messages.</p> <h3 id=\"data-loading\">Data loading</h3> <p>On page load, sites reads connected data using the visitor's connection and permissions. Sites manages caching and reloading; ask ChatGPT Work or Codex to add a manual refresh action if needed.</p> <p>By default, sites uses a <strong>Load more</strong> action to fetch another page when the connector returns a cursor.</p> <p><a id=\"technical-reference-plugin-discovery\"></a> <strong>Technical reference: Plugin discovery</strong></p> <p>Sites uses <code>getContext()</code> to find a plugin's actions. It returns cached tool names, descriptions, and schemas; it doesn't refresh discovery.</p> <p>For supported connected-app actions and availability, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339-creating-and-using-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and using ChatGPT Sites (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <h3 id=\"let-visitors-choose-their-connections\">Let visitors choose their connections</h3> <p>To use connected features, a visitor signs in with ChatGPT, reviews the app access the site requests, chooses the connected account and access to allow, and returns to the site. Sharing the site doesn't grant access to your connected accounts. The site receives data from the apps each visitor allows.</p> <p>Visitors can continue without granting app access, but features that need it won't work. If an app is unavailable, check that it's connected in the right workspace and allowed by workspace settings.</p>"};
